JointTag shows a joint log as a traceability tag hanging from the joint it records: a polypropylene pipe in side view, fused at a double-rolled bead, runs off both page edges, and the tag on its wire carries one form box per log field, each field's number pinned on the part of the joint it describes.

- On the site: a `table` block with `"look": "joint-tag"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-joint-tag.js`), svc-fabrication "One joint, one log line" (back on the page in pass 12 round C with `"seam": "plain"`; RecordSlips stays in the library). No concept of its own (Gemini quota); adapted from `research/pass9/concepts/sys-pw.4.png` (tags as physical objects) and the macro weld of `industries.1.v2.png`.
- Markup: `section.aq-joint-tag-sec` → `div.aq-joint-tag`: `__pipe` (aria-hidden svg: `__body`, `__shade`, `__hi`, `__edge`, `__fuse`, `__bead`, `__curl`, `__seam`, `__print` lot markings, `__sten` joint number, `__cut` and `__cutm` cut-out line, `__wire`, `g.__coupon` (the fused test coupon on its `__bench`: `__cb`, `__cs`, `__ce`, `__cbd`), `g.__pin` per field with `data-k`) and `__tag` (light paper, `data-theme="light"` and `data-paper`, dimmed in the dark theme): `__eye`, `p.__th` (column legend, aria-hidden), the fold wrapper with `ol.__fields` of `li.__field` (`data-k`): `aq-index`, `h3.__name`, `__proves` (`__k--sr` label), `__rec` (`__k`, the record on a dashed fill-in line).
- Fields, as a table: `cols` [field, what it proves, record], `rows`, `fold`, `fold_noun`. Optional `parts` (one per row: `num`, `lot`, `welder`, `bead`, `visual`, `coupon`, `sign`, `cut`; default from the field's words). The fold applies on phones only: on desktop the tag is the whole log line.
- Seam `"plain"` (look-only field, pass 12 round C, ruling RC2): the joint drawn method-neutral while FD-18 (the joining method) is open. One continuous length with a hairline girth line (`__girth`, bowed slightly so it reads round the pipe) and the stencilled joint number beside it; no `__fuse`, `__bead`, `__curl`, `__seam` and no coupon. The root gets `aq-joint-tag--plain`; the pins of the undrawn parts move onto the joint (parameters at the girth line's top, visual, test joint, welder and sign-off in one row under it, either side of the wire, clear of the tag's top edge; the joint number's pin a little higher, clear of the stencil). Fix round: on phones (≤600) the plain seam's stencil draws 1.3 x (about 13 px); at 601-860 the drawing crops at 140 % with 18-unit pins and the fields run two to a row; in dark the pin rings and cut marks take light ink. Used on svc-fabrication block 0; the fused default stays for a page that names its method.
- Tokens: the pipe is `limestone` with `on-limestone` mixes (an object, the same in both themes); tag `surface-raised` with `line` rules; pins `navy`, lit `flow`; field hover `flow-tint`.
- Pointing at or focusing into a field lights its pin.
- Phones: the drawing re-cropped round the joint (190 % wide), the tag full width, fields in one column with their labels.

## Motion

Motion: one timeline. The two lengths slide in from the edges and meet, the bead rolls up out of the seam, the lot markings print and the joint number is sprayed on, the wire draws round the joint, the tag drops on it and swings to rest, the pins land and the fields print box by box. With seam `"plain"` the one length slides in from the left, its girth line draws down and the number is sprayed on, then the wire, tag, pins and fields as above. About 4 s; nothing under reduced motion.
